# Audit-repair impact protocol

Preserve v053 and the supplied audit unchanged. Apply repairs to a new source tree. Freeze PLAN.json after repair tests and before the fresh replay; do not reuse v053 checkpoints as fresh v054 measurements.

Recompute the full v053 preparation route in each engine at N4 and N6: A=0→0.2 (eight intervals), then B=0→−0.25 (ten intervals), holding T=0, phi=0, ratio=0.8, theta=1.05, eps=0.003 and the declared constant tunnelling model. Retain the original residual, separation, jump, reality, isolation, basis, charge mesh/radius, spatial mesh, parameter-frame and endpoint-join gates. Qualify N4 before N6. There are 76 primary states and 36 fine/coarse parameter-orientation checks.

The impact wrapper replaces eleven suspect/legacy measurement surfaces with counting functions that raise if called. This tests actual non-use during the complete replay, rather than inferring execution from imports. All fresh computations still use the repaired Hamiltonian engine modules. Normal success/failure is recorded independently of the trap counters; every accepted case must start without saved steps, complete the route, and retain its guard record.

Revalidate new and old records, compare all 76 root pairs within 1e-6, compare saved two-planes with minimum overlap above 0.999999, and transform individual charges by the measured old/new frame signs. Record every spatial label change explicitly. Compare external-gap values without turning numerical agreement into an interval or physical-truth claim. Retain the original v044 anchor bytes and joins.

Finally run the complete test directory and bind the run to source, tests, input records and runtime. Report generation must revalidate this evidence and the impact comparison before it writes any output. Packaging verifies the preserved original tree and publication evidence under the declared extracted-tree contract. No prior ZIP is reconstructed or substituted.
